AMD-Faster - third party notices
================================

AMD-Faster is an independent, clean-room implementation. No source code was copied from Sodium,
Nvidium, Iris, VulkanMod, Mesa, LLVM or any AMD driver; those projects were studied for their public
design and their published behaviour, and the resulting ideas are re-implemented here from the
hardware documentation.

Ideas and constants that AMD-Faster does derive from published third party material:

* AMD RDNA / RDNA2 / RDNA3 / RDNA4 ISA Reference Guides, the RDNA Architecture Whitepaper and the
  GPUOpen performance guides: register file sizes, LDS sizes, wave32/wave64 rules, allocation
  granularities, occupancy behaviour, and the architecture/family classification in
  dev.amdfaster.core.arch.
* LLVM's AMDGPU backend (Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions) is used as the cross-check for the
  occupancy model: the formulas in dev.amdfaster.core.occupancy.OccupancyModel mirror
  AMDGPUBaseInfo.cpp::getNumWavesPerEUWithNumVGPRs() and the maxima in AMDGPU.td
  (FeatureMaxWavesPerEU*, Feature1536VGPRs).
* Mesa 3D (MIT) radeonsi/RADV/ACO sources were consulted for driver behaviour such as
  lds_size_per_workgroup and num_simd_per_compute_unit.
* PCI device ids in AmdGpuIdentifier are public hardware identifiers.

Bundled / optional components
-----------------------------
* LWJGL 3 (BSD-3-Clause) provides the Vulkan, VMA (Vulkan Memory Allocator), shaderc and SPIRV-Cross
  bindings used by the Vulkan backend. They are pulled from Maven Central and, when the mod is built
  with the natives embedded, redistributed unmodified inside the jar exactly as the LWJGL project
  ships them.
* AMD's LLVM based pipeline compiler (LLPC, MIT, GPUOpen-Drivers/llpc) is downloaded only when the
  optional offline ISA analysis is enabled (-PincludeAmdToolchain=true) and is redistributed
  unmodified with its own licence text in amdfaster-toolchain/. AMD-Faster works without it; the
  toolchain only adds offline shader/ISA analysis and pipeline precompilation.

